{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQhSLREAjoWH1xLWVWM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `Hijack()` so it only refuses once body bytes have been written. Calling it after only the headers were sent now works. All tests pass with `go test ./...`, and `go vet` and `gofmt` report nothing.\n\n**The bug:** `Hijack()` refused whenever the response counted as written. That includes the case where only the headers have gone out (for example after `WriteHeaderNow()`) and no body bytes have. WebSocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket` write the 101 status header and then hijack the connection, so they got `errHijackAlreadyWritten` under gin.\n\n**Changes in `response_writer.go`:**\n- `Hijack()` now checks for body bytes written instead of for any write at all:\n  - nothing written yet: allowed, and the writer is then marked as written (unchanged).\n  - only headers written: now allowed.\n  - body bytes written: still refused with `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n- I added a doc comment explaining this and naming the websocket library as the reason.\n- The error message is now `\"gin: response body already written\"`, so it says what actually blocks the hijack.\n\n**Tests in `response_writer_test.go`:** I added a case, \"hijack after header written should succeed\", to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`. The existing case that hijacking after a body write fails still passes.\n\nThe changes aren't committed yet. You're on a detached HEAD, so if you want a commit using your message as the title, tell me and I'll create a branch first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":33931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1023,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fcea2a3-1318-47d9-a49e-0703c594cb94","uuid":"b4bc2321-5fb0-4460-a16e-142e45bbf76b","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:26:06.673Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQhS8m1txb3ZqJyewUf"}
{"duration_api_ms":22835,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9fcea2a3-1318-47d9-a49e-0703c594cb94","total_cost_usd":0.1226246,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11413,"cache_read_input_tokens":119038,"output_tokens":2086,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":789},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11413},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":611,"cache_read_input_tokens":33931,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1023,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":2086,"cacheReadInputTokens":119038,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11413,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1226246,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":789,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed `Hijack()` so it only refuses once body bytes have been written. Calling it after only the headers were sent now works. All tests pass with `go test ./...`, and `go vet` and `gofmt` report nothing.\n\n**The bug:** `Hijack()` refused whenever the response counted as written. That includes the case where only the headers have gone out (for example after `WriteHeaderNow()`) and no body bytes have. WebSocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket` write the 101 status header and then hijack the connection, so they got `errHijackAlreadyWritten` under gin.\n\n**Changes in `response_writer.go`:**\n- `Hijack()` now checks for body bytes written instead of for any write at all:\n  - nothing written yet: allowed, and the writer is then marked as written (unchanged).\n  - only headers written: now allowed.\n  - body bytes written: still refused with `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n- I added a doc comment explaining this and naming the websocket library as the reason.\n- The error message is now `\"gin: response body already written\"`, so it says what actually blocks the hijack.\n\n**Tests in `response_writer_test.go`:** I added a case, \"hijack after header written should succeed\", to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`. The existing case that hijacking after a body write fails still passes.\n\nThe changes aren't committed yet. You're on a detached HEAD, so if you want a commit using your message as the title, tell me and I'll create a branch first.","ttft_ms":5339,"type":"result","duration_ms":27763,"uuid":"f795b42b-7930-4d74-a0aa-db54ac6bf291","ttft_stream_ms":2209,"time_to_request_ms":146,"first_content_frame_ms":2209,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
